WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.431
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Grammar, level B two.

2
00:00:05.731 --> 00:00:09.489
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.789 --> 00:00:16.586
Unit twenty-six: Cleft Sentences. Today you will highlight information with it-clefts and what-clefts.

4
00:00:16.886 --> 00:00:19.632
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:23.904
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:25.995
It was… that.

7
00:00:26.983 --> 00:00:29.343
It was… that means an it-cleft structure.

8
00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:31.566
It was Tom that called.

9
00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.907
Your turn. Say: It was… that.

10
00:00:37.767 --> 00:00:39.058
It was… that.

11
00:00:39.817 --> 00:00:40.806
What I need.

12
00:00:41.817 --> 00:00:43.956
What I need means a what-cleft beginning.

13
00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.969
What I need is rest.

14
00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:48.945
Your turn. Say: What I need.

15
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:52.952
What I need.

16
00:00:53.717 --> 00:00:54.753
The thing that.

17
00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:57.877
The thing that means an alternative cleft.

18
00:00:58.483 --> 00:00:59.926
The thing that annoys me.

19
00:01:00.517 --> 00:01:02.925
Your turn. Say: The thing that.

20
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:06.907
The thing that.

21
00:01:07.650 --> 00:01:08.639
All I want.

22
00:01:09.650 --> 00:01:12.335
All I want means a cleft meaning the only thing.

23
00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:14.497
All I want is peace.

24
00:01:15.083 --> 00:01:18.258
Your turn. Say: All I want.

25
00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.148
All I want.

26
00:01:22.883 --> 00:01:23.815
Focus.

27
00:01:24.817 --> 00:01:26.747
Focus means the main point.

28
00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:29.059
The focus is on time.

29
00:01:29.650 --> 00:01:32.059
Your turn. Say: Focus.

30
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:35.994
Focus.

31
00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:37.809
Emphasis.

32
00:01:38.817 --> 00:01:40.816
Emphasis means extra strength.

33
00:01:41.417 --> 00:01:42.789
Add emphasis.

34
00:01:43.383 --> 00:01:45.908
Your turn. Say: Emphasis.

35
00:01:48.767 --> 00:01:49.895
Emphasis.

36
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:51.454
Cleft.

37
00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:56.354
Cleft means split; a sentence divided to emphasise.

38
00:01:56.950 --> 00:01:58.369
A cleft sentence.

39
00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:01.601
Your turn. Say: Cleft.

40
00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:05.317
Cleft.

41
00:02:06.083 --> 00:02:07.189
Contrast.

42
00:02:08.183 --> 00:02:10.636
Contrast means a difference between things.

43
00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:12.518
A contrast.

44
00:02:13.117 --> 00:02:15.688
Your turn. Say: Contrast.

45
00:02:18.533 --> 00:02:19.488
Contrast.

46
00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.032
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.883 --> 00:02:27.858
Visal, say 'I need a rest' as a cleft sentence.

48
00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:40.696
What I need is a rest. A cleft sentence splits one idea into two parts to put focus on the important information. What I need is the first part, and a rest is the focus.

49
00:02:41.783 --> 00:02:43.110
What is an it-cleft?

50
00:02:44.217 --> 00:02:56.566
It was my brother who broke the window. It is the structure it + be + focus + that / who. It is used to correct or contrast: It wasn't Tom that called; it was Sara.

51
00:02:57.650 --> 00:02:59.023
What are other forms?

52
00:03:00.117 --> 00:03:14.605
All I want is some peace. The thing that annoys me is the noise. The place where we met was a cafe. Cleft sentences are common in speech and writing when we want to stress new or surprising information.

53
00:03:15.767 --> 00:03:17.464
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:18.317 --> 00:03:22.661
Grammar focus: Cleft sentences: It was… that and What… is.

55
00:03:22.961 --> 00:03:24.125
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:24.817 --> 00:03:26.596
What I need is a long rest.

57
00:03:27.483 --> 00:03:29.553
It was my brother who broke the window.

58
00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:32.647
All I want is some peace and quiet.

59
00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:41.744
It + be + focus + that / who… ; What / All + clause + be + focus. The cleft puts the important information last or in focus.

60
00:03:42.483 --> 00:03:45.635
Be careful! Don't say: It was Tom what called.

61
00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.437
Say: It was Tom who called.

62
00:03:49.737 --> 00:03:51.075
Use who for people.

63
00:03:51.867 --> 00:03:54.774
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:55.567 --> 00:03:56.951
Putting the Focus.

65
00:03:57.251 --> 00:03:59.088
What I need is a long rest.

66
00:04:00.100 --> 00:04:02.134
It was my brother who broke the window.

67
00:04:03.133 --> 00:04:05.179
All I want is some peace and quiet.

68
00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.097
The thing that annoys me is the noise.

69
00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:11.959
These sentences stress the main idea by contrast.

70
00:04:13.067 --> 00:04:17.254
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:04:18.117 --> 00:04:19.663
blank I need is a rest.

72
00:04:19.963 --> 00:04:23.152
A, What. B, That. C, Which.

73
00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:28.537
The answer is A: What.

74
00:04:29.683 --> 00:04:31.404
It was Tom blank called me.

75
00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:34.800
A, who. B, what. C, whose.

76
00:04:38.367 --> 00:04:40.134
The answer is A: who.

77
00:04:41.283 --> 00:04:43.039
All I want blank some peace.

78
00:04:43.339 --> 00:04:45.959
A, are. B, is. C, do.

79
00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:51.325
The answer is B: is.

80
00:04:52.483 --> 00:04:54.169
Why use a cleft sentence?

81
00:04:54.469 --> 00:04:58.947
A, to shorten. B, to ask. C, to focus on information.

82
00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:05.022
The answer is C: to focus on information.

83
00:05:06.183 --> 00:05:08.914
According to the reading, who broke the window?

84
00:05:09.214 --> 00:05:13.042
A, my brother. B, my sister. C, my friend.

85
00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.391
The answer is A: my brother.

86
00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:22.752
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:05:23.617 --> 00:05:27.021
Rewrite 'I need a rest' as a cleft sentence beginning 'What I need…'.

88
00:05:35.817 --> 00:05:37.410
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:50.640
What I need is a rest. A cleft sentence puts the focus on the important idea, and the sentence is stronger than 'I need a rest'. I can also say 'All I want is some quiet time'.

90
00:05:50.940 --> 00:05:52.661
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:05:53.550 --> 00:05:59.256
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and cleft sentences: it was… that and what… is.

92
00:05:59.556 --> 00:06:05.192
Today's value is eloquence. Choose your words with care, and speak to persuade honestly.

93
00:06:05.492 --> 00:06:08.307
See you in Unit twenty-seven. Goodbye!

94
00:06:08.607 --> 00:06:11.340
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

